new file mode 100644
index 0000000..099c652
--- /dev/null
+++ b/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+# smallpt · the browser edition
+
+Kevin Beason's C++ smallpt path tracer, compiled to WebAssembly with Emscripten. Open `index.html` through any static web host. The compiled artifacts are checked in; no build or rendering service is needed to use the app.
+
+The page starts a render automatically. Randomize colors changes the two colored walls and both small spheres, preserving mirror and glass materials. Quality and resolution changes restart the render. Reset restores the initial warm/teal palette and seed; Save image downloads a PNG of the current output. A pre-rendered image from the same WASM engine appears until the first complete pass is ready.
+
+## Rebuild
+
+Requires Emscripten (`emcc`) and Node.js:
+
+```sh
+npm run build
+npm test
+node scripts/render-preview.cjs # Optional: regenerate the 256 spp initial preview
+```
+
+`assets/render-worker.js` runs the compiled renderer in a dedicated Web Worker and transfers progressive RGBA frames to the canvas. Four camera samples per pixel are accumulated per pass, with small row batches for progress reporting. Starting another render terminates the previous worker. There are no rendering API requests, WebGL requirements, or cross-origin isolation requirements. Initial asset loads and optional Google Fonts require a network connection; rendering itself is entirely local.
+
+`vendor/smallpt/smallpt.cpp` is the unmodified upstream source from https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/smallpt.txt. `src/smallpt-wasm.cpp` adds allocation, palette, seeded rendering, and pixel-buffer exports while retaining the original radiance, ray/sphere intersection, and material functions. The initial palette is customized; the geometry is the original Cornell box scene. Upstream copyright and MIT license are in `vendor/smallpt/LICENSE.txt`.
+
+Validation uses the actual WASM binary in Node, without opening a browser or starting a server.
